# Personal/ephemeral files that land loose in the working tree (phone photos dropped for a
# quick look, ad-hoc screenshots, raw webcam capture frames) - never meant for a public repo.
# The repo went public 2026-08-06; before that these were just untracked and harmless, now
# an accidental `git add -A` would actually publish them. Pattern-based, not exact filenames,
# so the next one of these (different timestamp/ID) is caught automatically.
photo_*.jpg
photo_*.jpeg
docs/Screenshot_*.png
Screenshot_*.png
experiments/webcam/

# Calibration captures (photos/videos of the LEDs, the headset, the bench).
# NEVER committed: the repo is public and a lab photo can carry something personal in the frame
# without anyone noticing at upload time. The NUMBERS live in docs/ and in docs/pruebas.jsonl, which is
# the only reproducible part; the original file stays outside the tree (T230).
docs/led-photometry/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.heic
# Naming convention for anything that DOES belong in the tree: docs/32, "Naming captures".
# Short version: kebab-case, no spaces, the name says what it shows, never a clock time.
